# Template for secrets.bndrun, which is deliberately NOT in git (see .gitignore next to this
# file). Copy it, fill in the key, and run.launch picks it up through the optional
# `-include: -secrets.bndrun` in launch.bndrun:
#
#     cp secrets.bndrun.template secrets.bndrun
#
# Everything here arrives as a system property. configs/config.json in
# …mapping.local.config reads each value as $[env:NAME;default=$[prop:NAME;default=…]], so an
# exported environment variable takes precedence over what is set here, and a value left out
# falls back to the default in that file. Nothing in this chain ever puts a credential in git.
#
# Without this file the runtime starts exactly as before: model inference activates, finds no
# usable key, and records an UNAVAILABLE receipt on the first unknown payload.
#
# METAMODEL_MCP_URL must be reachable FROM ANTHROPIC, not from this machine. The Claude client
# sends the endpoint as an `mcp_servers` entry of type `url` (beta header mcp-client-2025-11-20),
# so the API connects to the MCP server itself - a localhost URL is never dialled from here and
# simply fails at request time. Expose the metamodel runtime's servlet (8099 by default, see
# emf.osgi-mcp's emf.runtime.config) over public HTTPS - an ngrok/cloudflared tunnel is enough
# for a test - and put that URL here, path included.
#
# METAMODEL_MCP_TOKEN must then match `auth.token` on that servlet's HttpMCPServerComponent
# configuration. The MCP server's McpAuthenticationFilter trusts direct loopback callers only
# while no token is configured, and a tunnelled request is loopback *with* a forwarding header,
# which it deliberately refuses ("Remote access requires a configured authentication token").
# So exposing the endpoint and setting a token are one step, not two: Anthropic presents it as
# `Authorization: Bearer <token>` when it calls the server.
#
# Not listed below, but overridable the same way: EVENTATLAS_CODEC_TYPE_MAP_ID, which must match
# the `http://eclipse.org/fennec/codec/typeMapping/{id}` annotation source the models this
# runtime loads actually carry. It defaults to `jena-sensors` (the m5airq/waterparc family) in
# config.json; set it here when you load a model set annotating for something else - the
# lorawan/em310udl fixtures use `lorawan`. An id no deployed model annotates for types nothing,
# and does so silently.
-runvm.secrets: \
	-DANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-REPLACE-ME,\
	-DMETAMODEL_MCP_URL=https://REPLACE-ME.example.dev/mcp/inference,\
	-DMETAMODEL_MCP_TOKEN=REPLACE-ME,\
	-DINFERENCE_NAMESPACE=https://fennec.eclipse.org/event.atlas/inferred,\
	-DINFERENCE_MODEL=claude-opus-5,\
	-DINFERENCE_MAX_RUNS=1,\
	-DINFERENCE_DOWNLOAD_FOLDER=/tmp/eventatlas-inference,\
	-DSAMPLING_MAX_WAIT=300
